      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m actually looking for some tips on how to prepare for a trip to New York. Any ideas on what I should start with?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to prepare for a trip to New York?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To prepare for your trip to New York City, start with these essential tips:\n\n1. **Plan Your Itinerary**: Research the top attractions you want to visit, such as Central Park, Times Square, and museums. Consider creating a daily itinerary that includes travel times and nearby dining options.\n\n2. **Transportation**: Purchase a seven-day unlimited MetroCard for the subway, which costs $33 USD plus a $1 fee for the card. This will allow you to travel easily around the city without worrying about individual fares.\n\n3. **Comfortable Footwear**: Since you may walk a lot (up to 10 miles a day), wear comfortable shoes to keep your feet happy throughout your adventures.\n\n4. **Packing Essentials**: Bring a mix of clothing suitable for the season, a portable charger for your phone, and a paper map of NYC in case your phone runs out of battery. An unlocked phone can also be useful for local SIM cards.\n\n5. **Timing**: Start your days early to avoid crowds at popular attractions. If you plan to visit museums, try to arrive when they open to avoid long lines.\n\n6. **Budgeting",
