      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Ah, that sounds more like my vibe! By the way, what\u2019s so special about New York\u2019s subway system?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is so special about New York's subway system?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "New York's subway system is special for several reasons. First, it is one of the oldest and largest public transit systems in the world, having opened in 1904 and featuring 472 stations across Manhattan, Brooklyn, Queens, and the Bronx. It operates 24/7, making it one of the few subway systems globally with round-the-clock service. \n\nThe subway handles over 1.7 billion rides annually, averaging about 5.6 million rides on weekdays. It connects diverse neighborhoods, providing access to various parts of the city without segregated fares\u2014one flat fare allows unlimited travel regardless of distance. \n\nAdditionally, the subway is a cultural melting pot, reflecting the city's diversity, and it plays a crucial role in New York's economy by facilitating the daily commute of millions. Despite its age and some safety concerns, it remains a vital and iconic part of New York City life, connecting people from all walks of life.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0008-79-03953:19": 2.3618812561035156,
