      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting! Do you know if there are any Spanish-themed neighborhoods or popular spots for Spanish culture in New York?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some places to visit in New York City that are closer to the Spanish culture?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "New York City has several neighborhoods and spots that celebrate Spanish culture. One of the most notable is **Little Spain**, located primarily along West 14th Street in Manhattan. This area was historically a hub for Spanish immigrants and features cultural institutions like the **Spanish Benevolent Society**. Although its prominence has diminished over the years, it still holds cultural significance.\n\nAdditionally, you can explore **Mercado Little Spain** at Hudson Yards, a food hall created by Chef Jos\u00e9 Andr\u00e9s that offers a variety of Spanish cuisine through its restaurants and food vendors. \n\nFor a more traditional experience, check out **Casa Moneo**, which was a key establishment in the Spanish culinary scene for decades, and **El Museo del Barrio**, which, while focused on Latin American culture, often includes Spanish influences in its exhibitions. \n\nLastly, the **Loisaida Center** in the East Village is another great spot that hosts events celebrating Latinx culture, including Spanish heritage. These locations will give you a rich taste of Spanish culture in NYC!",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0033-89-11446:4": 0.9163604974746704,
            "clueweb22-en0011-89-10290:8": 0.4411202073097229,
            "clueweb22-en0011-89-10290:0": 0.4348371624946594
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I live in Spain"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s awesome! Switching gears a bit\u2014can you recommend some places in New York City where I can train for my 10km race?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you recommend some places in New York City where I can train for my 10km race?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "In New York City, there are several great places to train for your 10km race:\n\n1. **Central Park**: With its scenic paths and varying terrain, Central Park is a favorite among runners. The loop around the park is approximately 6 miles, making it perfect for your training distance.\n\n2. **Prospect Park**: Located in Brooklyn, Prospect Park offers a beautiful 3.35-mile loop with rolling hills and a quieter atmosphere compared to Central Park.\n\n3. **The Hudson River Greenway**: This dedicated running path runs along the Hudson River, providing stunning views and a flat surface, ideal for speed work.\n\n4. **Brooklyn Bridge Park**: This area offers a mix of waterfront views and park paths, making it a scenic spot for training runs.\n\n5. **Van Cortlandt Park**: Located in the Bronx, this park has trails and a cross-country course that can add variety to your training.\n\n6. **The East River Esplanade**: This waterfront path along the East River is great for long runs with beautiful views of the skyline.\n\nThese locations will provide you with ample space and scenery to prepare for your race effectively!",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0046-51-15558:0": 1.5010203123092651,
