          "text": "New York City has several neighborhoods and spots that celebrate Spanish culture. One of the most notable is **Little Spain**, located primarily along West 14th Street in Manhattan. This area was historically a hub for Spanish immigrants and features cultural institutions like the **Spanish Benevolent Society**. Although its prominence has diminished over the years, it still holds cultural significance.\n\nAdditionally, you can explore **Mercado Little Spain** at Hudson Yards, a food hall created by Chef Jos\u00e9 Andr\u00e9s that offers a variety of Spanish cuisine through its restaurants and food vendors. \n\nFor a more traditional experience, check out **Casa Moneo**, which was a key establishment in the Spanish culinary scene for decades, and **El Museo del Barrio**, which, while focused on Latin American culture, often includes Spanish influences in its exhibitions. \n\nLastly, the **Loisaida Center** in the East Village is another great spot that hosts events celebrating Latinx culture, including Spanish heritage. These locations will give you a rich taste of Spanish culture in NYC!",
