    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m looking for advice on how to prepare for a trip to New York. Any tips on what to keep in mind before going?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to prepare for a trip to New York?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To prepare for your trip to New York City, here are some essential tips to keep in mind:\n\n1. **Plan Your Itinerary**: Make a rough plan of the places you want to visit, but allow for some spontaneity. It's easy to get caught up in the schedule, so leave time for unexpected discoveries.\n\n2. **Transportation**: Familiarize yourself with the subway and bus systems, as they are the most efficient ways to navigate the city. Consider how you'll get from the airport to your accommodation.\n\n3. **Packing**: Bring comfortable shoes, as you'll be doing a lot of walking. A light jacket can be useful, even in summer, as some indoor places can be quite cool.\n\n4. **Museum Visits**: Avoid visiting more than two museums in a single day to prevent fatigue. If you plan to visit popular attractions, arrive early to beat the crowds.\n\n5. **Stay Hydrated and Energized**: Look up nearby coffee shops or eateries in the neighborhoods you\u2019ll be exploring. Having a few pit stops in mind can help when you need a break.\n\n6. **Weather Considerations**: The best times to visit",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0046-73-02389:1": -0.6440839767456055
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I prefer using cash over cards for small purchases",
            "I like to have a nap during lunchtime"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Can you give me some information about the Metropolitan Museum of Art and other ones in New York City?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some information about the Metropolitan Mueseum of Art and other ones in New York City?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The Metropolitan Museum of Art, commonly known as \"The Met,\" is the largest art museum in the United States, located at 1000 Fifth Avenue, New York City. It was founded in 1870 and features a vast collection of over two million works of art, spanning 5,000 years of world culture, including pieces from ancient Egypt, European masters, and modern art. The museum is divided into 17 curatorial departments and offers a variety of exhibits, making it a must-visit for art enthusiasts. Admission is free for New York State residents, while other visitors pay a suggested fee.\n\nIn addition to The Met, New York City hosts several other notable museums:\n\n1. **American Museum of Natural History**: Located on the Upper West Side, it features exhibits on natural history, including dinosaurs and human cultures.\n\n2. **The Museum of Modern Art (MoMA)**: Renowned for its collection of modern and contemporary art, located in Midtown Manhattan.\n\n3. **The Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum**: Famous for its unique architectural design by Frank Lloyd Wright, it focuses on modern and contemporary art.\n\n4. **The Cloisters**: A branch of The Met located in Fort Try",
          "citations": {
