      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting, I always get lost in subways! Are there any places in New York City that remind people of Spain or its culture?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some places to visit in New York City that are closer to the Spanish culture?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, there are several places in New York City that celebrate Spanish culture and heritage. One notable spot is **Mercado Little Spain** at Hudson Yards, created by Chef Jos\u00e9 Andr\u00e9s. This food hall features various Spanish vendors and restaurants, offering a wide range of Spanish dishes and products, making it a great place to experience Spanish cuisine.\n\nAnother significant area is **Little Spain**, located primarily along West 14th Street, which historically served as a cultural hub for Spanish immigrants. Although it has diminished over the years, it still retains elements of its vibrant past, including the Spanish Benevolent Society, which represents the community's history.\n\nAdditionally, you might explore the **Boqueria** restaurants in Midtown and other locations, which bring the flavors of Spain to New York through tapas and traditional dishes. These locations provide a taste of Spain's culinary traditions and are perfect for anyone looking to immerse themselves in Spanish culture while in the city.",
