  {
    "runtag": "genaius-summary-rewrite",
    "type": "ikat-dialog-v1",
    "topic": "4-2",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m planning a trip to New York. Any idea what I should do first to get ready?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to prepare for a trip to New York?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To get started with your New York trip planning, consider these essential steps: First, decide on your budget and the length of your stay. Comfortable walking shoes and a MetroCard for the subway are must-haves, as you'll likely cover a lot of ground. Research neighborhoods to find the best area to stay based on your interests and proximity to attractions. For sightseeing, prioritize iconic landmarks like the Statue of Liberty, Empire State Building, and Central Park. If you're on a budget, the Staten Island Ferry offers free views of the Statue of Liberty. Lastly, plan your itinerary to balance famous spots with unique local experiences. A paper map or a digital one can be helpful for navigation. Enjoy your trip!",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0019-60-14092:5": 18.457599639892578,
            "clueweb22-en0017-05-13815:0": 18.200899124145508,
            "clueweb22-en0019-60-14092:11": 16.763200759887695
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That sounds helpful, thanks! I\u2019m really curious about museums there, especially the Metropolitan Museum of Art and others. Can you tell me something about them?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some information about the Metropolitan Mueseum of Art and other ones in New York City?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The Metropolitan Museum of Art, often called \"The Met,\" is one of the most iconic museums in New York City and a must-visit for art enthusiasts. Located on Fifth Avenue along Museum Mile, it houses over 2 million works spanning 5,000 years of history. Highlights include its vast collections of European paintings, Egyptian artifacts, and modern art. A unique piece to look out for is \"William the Faience Hippopotamus,\" a charming mascot of the museum from ancient Egypt. \n\nIf you\u2019re interested in exploring more museums, the Museum of Modern Art (MoMA) is another excellent choice, showcasing modern and contemporary art, while the American Museum of Natural History offers fascinating exhibits on science and nature. For a quieter experience, the Frick Collection and The Met Cloisters, which focuses on medieval art, are also worth considering. Let me know if you'd like tips on planning your visit!",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0008-68-12725:0": 31.160400390625,
            "clueweb22-en0001-88-13758:0": 30.115800857543945,
            "clueweb22-en0015-63-18755:0": 30.471200942993164
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I prefer quiet museums to crowded festivals."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I love that the Met has all those quiet, interesting spaces. Do you know anything interesting about New York\u2019s subway system?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is so special about New York's subway system?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The New York City subway system is fascinating! It\u2019s the largest rapid transit system in the world, with 472 stations spanning all five boroughs. It\u2019s also the busiest in the Western Hemisphere, serving as a lifeline for millions of New Yorkers daily. Interestingly, the subway tracks, if laid end-to-end, would stretch all the way from New York City to Chicago! Another quirky fact is the \"Pizza Principle,\" which observes that the price of a subway ride has historically been about the same as the cost of a slice of pizza. This unique system has been operating since 1904 and continues to evolve, making it an integral part of the city\u2019s history and culture.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0032-10-04300:0": 22.673099517822266,
            "clueweb22-en0032-10-04300:1": 20.615999221801758,
            "clueweb22-en0037-13-07838:0": 19.927799224853516
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I prefer quiet museums to crowded festivals."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s cool! Speaking of culture, are there places in New York that have a Spanish vibe or influence? Maybe neighborhoods, restaurants, or bookstores?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some places to visit in New York City that are closer to the Spanish culture?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "New York City offers several spots with a Spanish vibe or influence that you might enjoy. For neighborhoods, East Harlem, also known as El Barrio, is a hub of Puerto Rican culture and has a rich Latino heritage. You\u2019ll find vibrant murals, cultural institutions, and authentic eateries there. For dining, Tomino - Taberna Gallega in SoHo serves Spanish cuisine and is highly rated. Another option is Havana Central in Times Square, which offers Spanish and Latin American dishes with live music for a lively atmosphere. If you\u2019re looking for a unique bookstore experience, Librer\u00eda Donceles is a pop-up Spanish-language bookstore that celebrates the cultural dimension of the Spanish language and its diaspora. These spots should give you a taste of Spain while exploring the city!",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0038-22-10530:5": 22.52400016784668,
            "clueweb22-en0000-24-17120:0": 22.30699920654297,
            "clueweb22-en0006-93-05410:1": 22.244699478149414,
            "clueweb22-en0034-62-02336:0": 21.896799087524414
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I live in Spain."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Awesome, I might check out that bookstore! Now, can you recommend some places in New York City where I can train for my 10km race?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you recommend some places in New York City where I can train for my 10km race?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For training for your 10km race in New York City, I recommend checking out Van Cortlandt Park in the Bronx. It\u2019s a popular spot for runners, offering several miles of paths and trails, including cross-country routes. The park is spacious and provides a mix of terrains, making it ideal for building endurance and preparing for race conditions. Additionally, Central Park is another excellent option, with its well-maintained running loops and scenic views. Both locations are accessible and frequented by runners of all levels, so you\u2019ll feel motivated and part of a community.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0029-98-01019:0": 20.36910057067871
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I am not very confident in my fitness level."
