    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I love that the Met has all those quiet, interesting spaces. Do you know anything interesting about New York\u2019s subway system?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is so special about New York's subway system?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The New York City subway system is fascinating! It\u2019s the largest rapid transit system in the world, with 472 stations spanning all five boroughs. It\u2019s also the busiest in the Western Hemisphere, serving as a lifeline for millions of New Yorkers daily. Interestingly, the subway tracks, if laid end-to-end, would stretch all the way from New York City to Chicago! Another quirky fact is the \"Pizza Principle,\" which observes that the price of a subway ride has historically been about the same as the cost of a slice of pizza. This unique system has been operating since 1904 and continues to evolve, making it an integral part of the city\u2019s history and culture.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0032-10-04300:0": 22.673099517822266,
