      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m looking for advice on getting ready for a trip to New York. What should I do before going?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to prepare for a trip to New York?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To get ready for New York, start by checking the weather forecast, as the city experiences all four seasons and conditions can change quickly\u2014layered clothing is recommended for comfort [DOC-1]. Pack comfortable walking shoes, as you'll likely explore a lot on foot, and bring essentials like toiletries, personal medicines, and chargers. It's also wise to print hotel reservations and tickets for attractions or tours you plan to visit [DOC-1]. For getting around, familiarize yourself with the MetroCard system for subways and buses, which is convenient and cost-effective for visitors [DOC-2]. Before you leave, review a pre-trip checklist that includes travel documents, airport transfers, and a rough itinerary of must-see spots and activities [DOC-3]. Planning ahead will help you stay organized and make the most of your time in the city. Are you interested in recommendations for museums or quieter attractions in New York?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0024-42-09229:2": 0.04351873814041746,
