      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That sounds perfect, thanks! Now, what is so special about New York's subway system?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is so special about New York's subway system?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The New York City subway system stands out as the largest rapid transit system globally, with 472 stations spanning all five boroughs, making it a lifeline for millions of New Yorkers and visitors alike [clueweb22-en0032-10-04300:1]. It operates 24 hours a day, a rarity among major world cities, and is part of the Metropolitan Transportation Authority, the largest transportation network in North America [clueweb22-en0037-13-07838:0]. The subway's history dates back to 1904, and it was formed from the merger of three separate systems, reflecting the city's growth and diversity [clueweb22-en0030-36-05152:0]. Its extensive reach, constant operation, and historical significance make it a unique and essential feature of New York City life. Would you like tips for using the subway as a visitor?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0032-10-04300:1": 0.0734900544518332,
