          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To get ready for your trip to New York, start by planning your itinerary and booking accommodations in advance, as the city can be expensive and busy, especially for first-time visitors [DOC-1]. Prepare all necessary travel documents, including your passport, visa (if required), and printed hotel or activity reservations [DOC-2]. Pack comfortable walking shoes, layered clothing suitable for the season, and personal toiletries; don't forget items like a phone charger, umbrella, and any medications you need [DOC-2]. Research transportation options from the airport and within the city, such as subways, buses, and taxis, to make your arrival and daily travel smoother [DOC-2]. If you're traveling on a budget, look for free or low-cost attractions and consider making a list of must-see sights and experiences to maximize your time and money [DOC-1][DOC-4]. Do you need advice on allergy-friendly dining options in NYC?",
