      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s not quite what I needed\u2014I want more details about the Metropolitan Museum of Art itself. What can I see there? And can you mention some other interesting museums in the city?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some information about the Metropolitan Mueseum of Art and other ones in New York City?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "At the Met, you can explore over 2 million works of art across 17 departments. Highlights include its vast European paintings collection (with works by El Greco and Goya), the American Wing, the Temple of Dendur in the Egyptian Art section, Assyrian Lamassu, Greek and Roman sculpture, historic armor, and the Costume Institute. The museum also offers virtual tours to help you plan your visit in advance [DOC-1][DOC-4]. Other notable museums in New York City are the American Museum of Natural History, famous for its dinosaur fossils and natural world exhibits; the Met Cloisters, which focuses on medieval art; and a range of specialty museums like the New York City Fire Museum, the Federal Reserve Bank Museum, and the Museum of Interesting Things for quirky collections [DOC-2][DOC-3][DOC-5]. Are you interested in quieter or less crowded museums in NYC?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0042-77-13613:4": 0.04431852869352869,
