      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful, thanks! Instead, could you tell me what is so special about New York\u2019s subway system?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is so special about New York's subway system?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The New York City subway system stands out as the largest rapid transit system in the world, featuring 472 stations that connect all five boroughs and serving as a lifeline for millions of New Yorkers daily [DOC-1][DOC-2]. Its iconic design, including the color-coded lines and Helvetica signage introduced by Massimo Vignelli, has influenced transit map design globally and makes navigation more intuitive for riders [DOC-3]. The subway is also full of quirky facts and hidden secrets, such as abandoned stations and unique station art, adding to its cultural mystique and historical significance [DOC-4]. Are you interested in subway history tours or art installations?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0032-10-04300:1": 0.07487757538160764,
            "clueweb22-en0032-10-04300:0": 0.05393653135588619,
            "clueweb22-en0037-62-03615:0": 0.049466382776308146,
            "clueweb22-en0000-60-17433:7": 0.04848904298589833
          },
