      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "The art installations sound cool! Can you suggest any subway stations with interesting art or history to check out?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some places to visit in New York City that are closer to the Spanish culture?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "If you're interested in subway art, the 14th Street\u2013Eighth Avenue station (served by the A, C, E, and L lines) is a must-see. It houses 'Life Underground' by Tom Otterness, a beloved installation of over 100 cast-bronze sculptures scattered throughout the platforms and stairways. These playful, cartoon-like figures depict scenes from everyday city life and social allegories, such as a woman carrying a giant subway token and a fare jumper crawling under a gate. The installation took over a decade to complete and is considered one of the most popular and imaginative public artworks in the subway system [DOC-1][DOC-5]. Are you interested in guided tours focused on subway art?",
          "citations": {
