          "user_rubrik": "Can you recommend some places in New York City where I can train for my 10km race?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The Hudson River Greenway is a favorite among runners, offering beautiful waterfront views and a route that can be tailored to your desired distance, including a 10km run. Starting around 14th Street and heading toward Lower Manhattan provides a scenic and relatively flat course, especially peaceful early in the morning or evening to avoid crowds [DOC-2]. Central Park is another iconic spot with multiple loops suitable for 10km training, and the East River paths are popular with locals and offer a quieter alternative [DOC-2]. NYC also has many parks\u2014over 1,700 in total\u2014so you can find peaceful green spaces for running, such as Prospect Park or Flushing Meadow Park [DOC-4]. If you prefer a predictable, flat surface, local running tracks are ideal for beginners and those looking to improve speed or technique [DOC-3]. For extra motivation or community, you might consider joining a local running group, many of which welcome beginners and offer supportive environments [DOC-1]. Would you like specific running route maps or directions in NYC?",
