          "text": "New York City has a rich Spanish and Hispanic heritage. Historically, 'Little Spain' on 14th Street in Manhattan was a vibrant center for Spanish immigrants and culture, as highlighted in the documentary 'Little Spain' [DOC-3]. For a taste of Spain, you can dine at acclaimed Spanish restaurants such as Tomi\u00f1o Taberna Gallega, Boqueria, and Victor's Cafe, which offer authentic tapas and Spanish dishes [DOC-5]. For book lovers, Librer\u00eda Donceles is a unique Spanish-language bookstore and art project that celebrates Spanish literature and culture [DOC-2]. Additionally, the city hosts the 116th Street Hispanic Festival, a major event celebrating Puerto Rican and broader Hispanic culture with food, music, and family activities [DOC-4]. Exploring these spots will give you a meaningful connection to Spanish heritage while in NYC. Would you like recommendations for specific Spanish restaurants or tapas bars?",
