      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m actually looking for advice about preparing for a trip to New York! What should I keep in mind?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to prepare for a trip to New York?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When visiting New York City, it's smart to buy a seven-day unlimited MetroCard for convenient and cost-effective travel on subways and buses, as public transportation is the easiest way to get around the city [DOC-3][DOC-2]. While you prefer using cash for small purchases, note that most places in NYC accept cards, even for small amounts, but having some cash is still useful for flea markets or small vendors [DOC-4]. Since you enjoy museums and quieter activities, prioritize world-class museums like the Met or MoMA, and consider exploring less crowded boroughs beyond Manhattan [DOC-3]. With your peanut allergy, always inform restaurant staff and check menus carefully, as NYC has a diverse food scene but cross-contamination can occur. Summer can be hot and humid, so dress comfortably and stay hydrated [DOC-4]. Finally, New Yorkers are direct but helpful\u2014don't hesitate to ask for directions if needed [DOC-1]. Are you interested in budget-friendly activities or free walking tours?",
          "citations": {
