          "user_utterance": "Maybe! But before that, what is so special about New York's subway system?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is so special about New York's subway system?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The New York City subway system stands out as the largest rapid transit system in the world, with 472 stations serving all five boroughs. It operates 24 hours a day, making it one of the few major subway systems globally to offer round-the-clock service. The subway opened in 1904 and has a rich history, with some lines using routes dating back to the 19th century. Its extensive network is a lifeline for New Yorkers and visitors alike, providing easy access to major attractions, museums, and neighborhoods. The system is also notable for its constant improvements, such as the modern Fulton Center transit hub, and its role as the busiest rapid transit system in the Western Hemisphere, carrying approximately 1.7 billion riders annually [DOC-1][DOC-2][DOC-3][DOC-4]. Do you want to know about subway safety and etiquette?",
