          "text": "New York\u2019s subway stands out for several reasons that directly impact your experience as a visitor:\n\n**What Makes NYC\u2019s Subway Unique**\n\n- **24/7 Operation:** Unlike most global systems, the subway runs all day, every day\u2014including late nights\u2014making it easy to get around at any hour (ideal if you want flexibility or avoid crowds by traveling off-peak) [clueweb22-en0037-13-07838; clueweb22-en0002-92-17118; clueweb22-en0009-20-19130].\n- **Unmatched Reach:** With 472 stations, it\u2019s the world\u2019s largest subway by number of stops, serving four boroughs (Manhattan, Brooklyn, Queens, Bronx). You can reach nearly any destination in the city without needing a taxi [clueweb22-en0032-10-04300; clueweb22-en0001-56-11006].\n- **Flat Fare, Simple Payment:** One fare ($2.75) covers any distance or transfer. MetroCard vending machines accept cash, matching your preference for",
