          "text": "For a relaxing spring visit to New York, here are the most notable events and experiences\u2014filtered for your preferences (quiet, cash-friendly, allergy-aware, and nap-friendly):\n\n**Best Spring Events & Experiences**\n\n- **Cherry Blossom Viewing at Brooklyn Botanic Garden**\n  - April is peak bloom; the Sakura Matsuri festival draws crowds, but you can visit on a weekday for a quieter stroll among cherry blossoms. The garden is spacious, ideal for a peaceful walk or rest. Tickets can be bought with cash at the gate.\n  - Food vendors are present\u2014always confirm ingredients due to your peanut allergy.\n\n- **Bryant Park & Central Park**\n  - Both parks host spring flower displays and occasional small events, but you\u2019ll find plenty of quiet corners for a nap, especially midday on weekdays.\n  - Nearby kiosks and cafes accept cash for snacks.\n\n- **Macy\u2019s Flower Show**\n  - Late March\u2013early April, Macy\u2019s Herald Square transforms with elaborate floral installations. Go early or on weekdays for a less crowded, visually stunning experience.\n\n- **Avoid Large Parades &",
