          "text": "Here\u2019s how to prepare for your New York trip, tailored to your preferences:\n\n**Money & Payments**\n- Cash is widely accepted for small purchases (e.g., street food, subway tickets, corner stores). ATMs are plentiful, but check for international withdrawal fees.\n- For the subway, buy a MetroCard (unlimited weekly pass is $33 + $1 for the card), which you can purchase with cash at vending machines.\n\n**Food & Allergies**\n- NYC is allergy-aware, but always double-check with staff about peanut ingredients, especially at food carts and bakeries.\n- Many restaurants list allergens; when in doubt, opt for chain restaurants or places with clear labeling.\n\n**Travel Logistics**\n- From Spain, ensure your passport and ESTA (visa waiver) are valid.\n- Airport transfers: Taxis, shuttle buses, and trains connect JFK/LGA/EWR to Manhattan. Cash is accepted for taxis.\n- Pack comfortable shoes\u2014expect to walk a lot.\n\n**Budget Tips**\n- NYC can be expensive, but there are many free/low-cost attractions (Central Park, ferry",
