          "text": "For a focused, rewarding visit to the Metropolitan Museum of Art\u2014especially if you prefer quieter, less crowded experiences\u2014prioritize these must-see highlights:\n\n**Top Must-See Masterpieces**\n- **The Temple of Dendur (Egyptian Art, Sackler Wing):** An ancient Egyptian temple bathed in natural light, often cited as the Met\u2019s most awe-inspiring space and generally less crowded than the European galleries.\n- **Assyrian Lamassu (Ancient Near Eastern Art):** Monumental winged guardians\u2014impressive and usually in a quieter section.\n- **Greek and Roman Sculpture Court:** Expansive, airy, and ideal for a peaceful stroll among classical statues.\n- **American Wing:** Includes period rooms and iconic works like John Singer Sargent\u2019s \u201cMadame X.\u201d These galleries are often calmer than the European painting halls.\n- **Arms and Armor:** Fascinating displays of historic armor and weaponry, popular but with plenty of space to move.\n\n**If You Have Extra Time**\n- **Islamic Art Galleries:** Recently renovated, featuring intricate tapestries",
