        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s really helpful! Switching topics a bit, what is so special about New York\u2019s subway system?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is so special about New York's subway system?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "New York's subway system is one of the world's oldest and most used metro systems, with the most metro stations. It runs 24 hours a day, 365 days a year, and has a total of 245 miles of routes. The system is also unique in that it has an extensive network of interconnected lines, allowing for more one-seat rides, but also making it more prone to delays. The subway system is a vital part of the city's infrastructure, with an average of 5.4 million rides per day, making it the busiest rapid transit system in the Western Hemisphere. Its complexity and size make it a remarkable feat of engineering and a iconic symbol of New York City.",
