          "text": "As a collector of rare books, you'll be delighted to know that New York has a treasure trove of unique bookshops and collections. The Rare Book Division at the New York Public Library is a must-visit, with its vast collection of rare and historic books. You can also explore the Argonaut Bookshop, which specializes in the history of California and the American West, or visit the Weiser Antiquarian Books, which focuses on occult and mystical texts. Additionally, the Mysterious Bookshop in New York City is a haven for mystery and crime fiction enthusiasts, with a wide range of rare and collectible books. These are just a few examples, and you're sure to discover many more hidden gems during your visit.",
