          "text": "New York's subway system is unique in that it is the largest in the world, with 472 stations that reach all five boroughs. It is also the busiest rapid transport system in the Western hemisphere, with an average of 5.4 million rides per day. The system operates 24 hours a day, making it a convenient mode of transportation for both locals and tourists. Additionally, the subway system has a rich history, with some of its stations featuring unique architecture and design. Overall, the New York subway system is an iconic and essential part of the city's infrastructure, making it a special and notable aspect of the city.",
