          "text": "New York\u2019s subway system is one of the largest and busiest in the world, with 472 stations serving four of the five boroughs. It operates 24/7, which is quite unique compared to many cities. The system covers a vast area, making it one of the most affordable and convenient ways to get around the city, especially if you prefer cash\u2014remember that MetroCards or OMNY contactless payments are accepted, but it\u2019s handy to carry some cash nearby for vending machines or small purchases. The subway offers a real glimpse into NYC\u2019s diverse culture, with street performers and unique art murals in many stations. Given your preference for quieter places, try traveling during off-peak hours to avoid crowds and have a more comfortable experience. Also, plan ahead using apps or maps to avoid getting overwhelmed. It\u2019s an essential part of the New York experience and great for exploring at your own pace while balancing activity and rest.",
