          "text": "When traveling to New York, it's essential to pack light and versatile clothing that can be easily mixed and matched. Consider bringing layers for the unpredictable weather, as well as comfortable shoes for walking. Don't forget to pack any necessary medications, such as allergy relief for your peanut allergy. Additionally, make sure to research and book your accommodations and transportation in advance to avoid any last-minute stress. It's also a good idea to have some local currency, the US dollar, for when you arrive. Lastly, consider purchasing travel insurance to protect yourself against any unexpected events.  (",
