        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s great, thanks. What\u2019s so special about New York\u2019s subway system?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is so special about New York's subway system?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The New York City subway system is special for several reasons: it's one of the world's oldest (opened 1904), largest by number of stations (472), and the busiest in the Western Hemisphere. It uniquely operates 24/7, connecting all neighborhoods with a uniform fare, and is considered the city's lifeblood, moving millions daily.",
