        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Cool! What are some places to visit in New York City that are closer to the Spanish culture?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some places to visit in New York City that are closer to the Spanish culture?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "New York City offers several places with Spanish cultural ties. You can explore Mercado Little Spain at Hudson Yards, a food hall by Chef Jos\u00e9 Andr\u00e9s focusing on Spanish cuisine, tapas, and a shop. For dining, consider restaurants like Boqueria or others listed as top Spanish restaurants. Historically, West 14th Street was known as \"Little Spain,\" home to Casa Moneo and Spanish-themed entertainment. You might also find Latin music venues.",
