        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That sounds so cool! What\u2019s so special about New York\u2019s subway system?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is so special about New York's subway system?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The New York City subway system is special for being one of the world's oldest (opened 1904), largest by stations (472), and most-used, uniquely operating 24/7. It's the busiest rapid transit system in the Western Hemisphere, with an expansive network whose tracks could stretch from NYC to Chicago if laid end-to-end. It's also unique for its extensive interlining.",
