        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Impressive, I didn\u2019t realize it was that big. Can you suggest places in New York City that have a Spanish vibe or link to Spanish history?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some places to visit in New York City that are closer to the Spanish culture?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "New York City offers several spots with a Spanish vibe or historical connection. West 14th Street was historically known as \"Little Spain,\" a vibrant Spanish-American neighborhood. You can still find the Spanish Benevolent Society there, and historically, Casa Moneo was a key Spanish food emporium, alongside the Church of Our Lady of Guadalupe. For a modern Spanish culinary experience, visit Mercado Little Spain at Hudson Yards. Spanish Harlem, or \"El Barrio,\" is another area with a strong Spanish-speaking community.",
