          "user_utterance": "Interesting! I might check Mercado Little Spain. Now, can you recommend some places in New York City where I can train for my 10km race?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you recommend some places in New York City where I can train for my 10km race?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For training for your 10km race in New York City, consider these popular routes:\n*   **Central Park:** Offers a 6-mile loop, plus shorter options and a loop around The Reservoir.\n*   **Hudson River Greenway:** A beautiful path along the water, up to 9 miles.\n*   **East River:** Great for longer runs, with options up to 16 miles.\n*   **Flushing Meadow Park:** Features a 4-mile course, popular for 10K races.\n*   **Brooklyn Bridge Park and Brooklyn Bridge:** Offers scenic runs with great views.\nYou could also look into the New Balance Bronx 10 Miler if you're interested in a local race.",
