          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "The Cloisters sounds very interesting, thanks! What is so special about New York's subway system?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is so special about New York's subway system?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "New York City's subway system is special for being one of the world's oldest (opened 1904), largest (472 stations), and busiest, carrying millions daily. It uniquely operates 24/7, 365 days a year, connecting all four boroughs it serves. It also features a flat fare, regardless of how far you travel, fostering a sense of equality as it links diverse neighborhoods.",
