          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "The Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met) is one of the world's largest and most visited art museums, so it can be quite bustling. However, its much smaller second location, The Cloisters, in Fort Tryon Park, contains an extensive collection of medieval European art and might offer a more serene experience. The provided information doesn't explicitly state which other museums are quiet. Could you tell me what kind of art or exhibits you prefer, or what \"quiet\" means to you (e.g., fewer crowds, contemplative atmosphere)?",
