      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! Can you say what makes the New York subway system special compared to other cities?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is so special about New York's subway system?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The New York City subway system is unique in several ways. It's one of the world's oldest, largest (with 472 stations), and the busiest in the Western Hemisphere. Unlike many other global systems, it operates 24/7. A key distinguishing feature is its flat fare, meaning the cost is the same regardless of distance, with no fare zones. It also has a distinct nomenclature, differentiating between physical \"lines\" and the \"services\" (routes) that run on them.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0012-89-04705:0": 0.4833088517189026,
