        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Ooh, Mercado Little Spain sounds yummy! Do you know if there are any good flea markets or rare book shops in NYC?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you recommend some places in New York City where I can train for my 10km race?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "For flea markets, consider the popular **Brooklyn Flea**, with locations in Williamsburg (Saturdays) and DUMBO (Sundays), known for vintage items and food. Other options include **LIC + Astoria Flea & Food** and **Nolita Market**. For rare books, check out **Helmut Lang: NY** for rare art photography books, or **Mast Books** in Alphabet City for a unique curation of art and film books.",
