      {
        "turn": 9,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s super helpful! Oh, and one more thing\u2014can you recommend some places in New York City where I can train for my 10km race?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you recommend some places in New York City where I can train for my 10km race?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For your 10km race training in New York City, you have several excellent options. Central Park offers a challenging 6-mile loop and a shorter loop around The Reservoir. Other great outdoor routes include the Hudson River Greenway along the West Side, East River paths, and Brooklyn Bridge Park. Flushing Meadow Park in Queens also has a 4-mile running course, which is a popular spot for 10K races. For dedicated indoor training, you could also consider places like the Mile High Run Club.",
