        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting, especially the 24/7 part. Are there any Spanish neighborhoods or Spanish cultural spots in New York I shouldn\u2019t miss?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some places to visit in New York City that are closer to the Spanish culture?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Given your interest in Spanish culture, you might explore the historical \"Little Spain\" area around West 14th Street in Manhattan, home to the Spanish Benevolent Society and the Church of Our Lady of Guadalupe. For a culinary experience, visit Mercado Little Spain at Hudson Yards, a food hall dedicated to Spanish cuisine, or try Boqueria, a Spanish restaurant with multiple locations. East Harlem, also known as \"El Barrio,\" is another historically significant Latino neighborhood.",
