      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Oh, I\u2019m actually curious\u2014what should I do to prepare for a trip to New York? Any essential tips?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to prepare for a trip to New York?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "here \u2019 s a quick prep - and - go guide for nyc from spain : - travel docs : valid passport + esta approval. consider travel insurance. - money : nyc is very card - centric, but carry small bills for street vendors / flea markets and tips ( 15 \u2013 20 % in restaurants ). - power / phone : us plugs are type a / b, 120v \u2014 bring an adapter. set up an esim / roaming. - getting around : you can tap to pay on subways / buses with a contactless card / phone. wear very comfy shoes \u2014 nyc means lots of walking. - packing : lightweight waterproof jacket, layers, small umbrella, portable charger, hand sanitizer, tissues. if summer bothers your nose, bring antihistamines / nasal spray. - food allergy : carry your epinephrine and a printed allergy card ( peanut allergy ). ask explicitly about cross \u2011 contamination. - reservations : book popular museums / statue of liberty / broadway ahead ; big places can have timed entry. - safety : use a zippered crossbody, keep phone secure, avoid empty subway cars late at night. - your vibes : - flea markets :",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0034-01-11945:1": -2.7054059505462646,
            "clueweb22-en0012-96-09870:0": -3.1195926666259766,
