      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "This is super helpful\u2014definitely noting the flea markets! Can you also give me some info about the Metropolitan Museum of Art and other museums in NYC?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some information about the Metropolitan Mueseum of Art and other ones in New York City?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "absolutely! here \u2019 s a quick museum guide, with the met first. metropolitan museum of art ( the met ) - highlights : temple of dendur ( egyptian ), american wing, arms & armor, impressionists, medieval art. - tips : buy timed tickets online. typically closed wednesdays ; open late fri \u2013 sat ( quieter ). check bags policy \u2014 large backpacks must be checked. - the met cloisters : included same - day ; a serene medieval branch in fort tryon park \u2014 great for a quiet visit. - allergy note : museum cafes may use nuts ; ask about cross \u2011 contact or eat just before / after your visit. other excellent museums - moma : picasso, warhol, rothko. reserve timed entry ; go at opening for fewer crowds. - american museum of natural history : dinosaurs, blue whale, planetarium. timed entry required. - 9 / 11 memorial & museum : powerful, plan 2 \u2013 3 hours ; book ahead. - whitney museum : modern american art ; river views ; friday evenings pay \u2011 what \u2011 you \u2011 wish. - guggenheim : iconic spiral building ; pay \u2011 what \u2011 you \u2011 wish saturday evenings. - morgan library & museum : illuminated manuscripts and rare books \u2014 perfect for",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0040-35-07998:1": -2.290891170501709,
            "clueweb22-en0028-88-01782:0": -2.2983574867248535,
            "clueweb22-en0030-37-04963:1": -2.3310816287994385,
            "clueweb22-en0028-90-15912:0": -2.5226423740386963,
            "clueweb22-en0029-42-06790:3": -3.021324634552002
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s awesome, thanks! I\u2019d love to see the Morgan Library, especially as a book collector. What\u2019s so special about New York\u2019s subway system, by the way?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is so special about New York's subway system?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "you \u2019 ll love the morgan library & museum as a book collector. it \u2019 s a historic gem with world - class manuscripts, rare books, and music scores, plus rotating exhibitions. it \u2019 s an easy walk from grand central ( madison ave at 36th st ) ; plan 1 \u2013 2 hours. expect galleries plus j. p. morgan \u2019 s historic library rooms, and a calm atmosphere. hours are generally mid \u2011 morning to late afternoon \u2014 check the day \u2019 s schedule and current exhibits before you go. if you \u2019 re sensitive to nut cross \u2011 contact, ask at the cafe or eat before / after. what \u2019 s special about nyc \u2019 s subway : - it runs 24 / 7 across four boroughs \u2014 one of the world \u2019 s largest systems. - flat fare and tap - to - pay ( omny ) with a contactless card / phone. - express vs. local trains : express skip stops ; always check the train letter / number and \u201c uptown / downtown. \u201d - weekend service changes are common \u2014 use an app like citymapper / transit or check station notices. - etiquette : let riders off first, move to the car \u2019 s center, don \u2019 t block doors, and avoid empty cars late at night",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0011-90-08832:13": -2.0199015140533447,
            "clueweb22-en0011-90-08832:1": -2.16334867477417,
