          "text": "great \u2014 practical picks and a simple plan. places to train - central park : varied terrain, the reservoir and cross \u2011 town loops are perfect for tempo and recovery runs. - prospect park ( brooklyn ) : a popular, car \u2011 free 3. 35 \u2011 mile loop ideal for long runs and steady miles. - hudson river park & waterfront esplanades : flat, long stretches for pace work and negative \u2011 split long runs. - brooklyn bridge park / riverside park : scenic routes for easy miles and cooldowns. - local tracks & high \u2011 school stadiums : use for interval / repeat sessions when you need precise distances. groups, stores & events - join group runs and clinics ( local running stores like jackrabbit regularly host pre \u2011 race group runs, demos and clinics ). look for community runs tied to races or brands. quick 8 \u2011 week training template ( if you already run 3 \u2013 4x / wk ) - 1 long run ( gradually build to 10 \u2013 12 miles ) - 1 speed session ( intervals or track ) - 1 tempo run ( race pace efforts ) - 1 \u2013 2 easy recovery runs + rest / cross \u2011 train tips : prioritize shoes, hydration, and subway access to start / finish runs safely",
