          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I'm thinking about visiting New York soon. What should I do to prepare for the trip?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to prepare for a trip to New York?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "nice idea \u2014 here are practical, personalized steps to prepare : - check entry rules : confirm passport validity, visa / esta and any covid or quarantine rules for travelers from spain. buy travel insurance. - book ahead : reserve timed tickets for quieter museums ( mornings or late afternoons ) and any guided tours to avoid crowds. - consider day trips carefully : a niagara falls day tour from nyc can be a 20 \u2011 hour outing ( options leave late night or early morning and include the maid of the mist ) ; it \u2019 s spectacular but tiring if you \u2019 re not very fit. - pack smart : comfortable walking shoes, layered clothing, universal adapter, phone charger, photocopies of documents, face masks if required. bring cash for small purchases. - health & food : carry your meds and an epipen if prescribed ( peanut allergy ), plus peanut \u2011 free snacks. - comfort : schedule downtime ( a lunchtime nap fits you well ) and plan low \u2011 impact activities. - home prep : tidy up, pause deliveries, and leave emergency contact info. if you want, tell me travel dates and interests ( quiet museums, rare \u2011 book hunting ) and i \u2019 ll suggest specific nyc spots and",
          "citations": {
