          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "great \u2014 here \u2019 s a focused plan for museum visits in nyc, tailored to your love of quieter spaces and rare books. metropolitan museum of art - one of the world \u2019 s largest encyclopedic museums, located on the east side of central park. expect vast collections ( ancient through modern ) and quieter corners if you avoid the main entrances and blockbuster exhibits. - tip : book a timed ticket in advance ( general adult tickets are around the $ 40 range ) and aim for weekday mornings or late afternoons for lower crowds. allow downtime ( cafes / benches ) between galleries. other museums you \u2019 ll enjoy - the morgan library & museum \u2014 ideal for manuscripts, rare books and intimate galleries ; perfect for a rare - book collector. - the frick collection \u2014 smaller, calmer, great for quieter viewing of old masters. - the museum of modern art ( moma ) and the whitney \u2014 excellent modern / contemporary art ; try weekday late afternoons. practical tips - buy timed / skip \u2011 the \u2011 line tickets or a city pass to avoid queues. - plan short visits with naps / rests between museums and choose weekdays when possible. tell me your dates and which neighborhoods you ' ll stay in and i \u2019 ll propose a day -",
          "citations": {
