      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! I\u2019ll probably stay in Manhattan. What\u2019s so special about New York\u2019s subway system?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is so special about New York's subway system?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Great choice\u2014staying in Manhattan makes the subway one of your best tools. What\u2019s special about it:  - Coverage and speed: a huge, fast network that links all five boroughs and puts most landmarks and museums a short ride away.   - 24/7 service: trains run overnight (though less frequently), so you have flexibility with late returns.   - Price: very affordable per ride; if you\u2019re staying several days, consider a multi-day/unlimited pass. You can buy MetroCards or pay with OMNY (contactless). If you prefer cash, station agents and some vending machines accept it.   - Express vs local: some trains skip stops\u2014use express for longer hops, local for short trips.   - Practical tips for you: avoid weekday rush hours (mornings and early evenings) for quieter rides; many stations lack elevators, so plan routes if you want to minimize stairs; check for weekend service changes before traveling.   - Apps: use Google Maps or Citymapper for real\u2011time routes and alerts.  If you tell me your dates/where you\u2019ll stay, I can suggest the easiest lines for museum visits.",
          "citations": {
